===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*welH-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|wal}}, from {{inh|en|ang|weall|t=wall, dike, earthwork, rampart, dam, rocky shore, cliff}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*wall|t=wall, rampart, entrenchment}}, from {{der|en|la|vallum|t=wall, rampart, entrenchment, palisade}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*welH-|t=to turn, wind, roll}}. Perhaps conflated with {{m|en|waw|t=a wall within a house or dwelling, a room partition}}, from {{noncog|enm|wawe}}, from {{noncog|ang|wāg}}, {{m|ang|wāh|t=an interior wall, divider}}, see {{l|en|waw}}. Cognate with {{cog|frr|wal|t=wall}}, {{cog|stq|Waal|t=wall, rampart, mound}}, {{cog|nl|wal|t=wall, rampart, embankment}}, {{cog|de|Wall|t=rampart, mound, embankment}}, {{cog|sv|vall|t=mound, wall, bank}}. More at {{l|en|wallow}}, {{l|en|walk}}.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia|mul=wall (butterfly)}}
